    {
      "id": "p0219-b010",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "After this, the translator changed the \"Turn\" command into hikkuri kaesu (\"to flip over or around\"). The resulting Japanese localization closely parallels Toby's original design: the first Japanese command does nothing, the second command looks similar to the first command at first glance, and the second command also causes Mettaton to be turned around.",
        "raw": "After this, the translator changed the \"Turn\" command into hikkuri kaesu (\"to\nflip over or around\"). The resulting Japanese localization closely parallels\nToby's original design: the first Japanese command does nothing, the second\ncommand looks similar to the first command at first glance, and the second\ncommand also causes Mettaton to be turned around.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
